---
// biome-ignore lint/correctness/noUnusedImports: Astro uses this layout component below.
import SiteLayout from "../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
---

<SiteLayout
  title="Privacy | plansplease"
  description="How plansplease handles local snapshots and cloud HTML uploads in the alpha."
  activePath="privacy"
>
  <section class="page-heading" aria-labelledby="privacy-title">
    <div>
      <h1 id="privacy-title">Your pages are yours.</h1>
      <p>
        We believe developers and makers should maintain complete ownership and control over the
        code, documents, and tools their AI agents create.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="privacy-content">
    <div class="privacy-grid">
      <article class="privacy-card">
        <h3>Cloud pages belong to your account</h3>
        <p>
          Files uploaded to the cloud workspace are tied strictly to your authenticated GitHub
          account. Your dashboard only lists your account's documents, and nobody else can browse
          your library.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="privacy-card">
        <h3>Cloud previews require your session</h3>
        <p>
          In the current alpha, preview requests verify your active session token before returning
          the stored HTML. Private artifacts are protected by default.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="privacy-card">
        <h3>Local pages stay on your machine</h3>
        <p>
          The CLI binds its daemon strictly to the loopback interface (<code>127.0.0.1</code>).
          Local snapshots are served entirely on your hardware and never touch external servers.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="privacy-card">
        <h3>Uploads start with standalone HTML</h3>
        <p>
          The cloud upload flow currently accepts standalone HTML files. Multi-asset folders and
          complex project bundles will be supported as we scale object storage capabilities.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>

    <p class="page-note">
      This privacy summary will be expanded into comprehensive enterprise terms as plansplease
      moves towards general availability.
    </p>
  </section>
</SiteLayout>

<style>
  .privacy-content {
    padding: 3.5rem 0 5rem;
  }

  .privacy-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 1.75rem;
  }

  .privacy-card {
    padding: 2.25rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--night-border);
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
    background: var(--night-card);
  }

  .privacy-card h3 {
    margin: 0 0 0.75rem;
    color: var(--text-white);
    font-family: var(--display);
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .privacy-card p {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--night-muted);
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .privacy-card code {
    padding: 0.15rem 0.35rem;
    border-radius: 4px;
    background: var(--night-soft);
    border: 1px solid var(--night-border);
    color: var(--mint);
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 0.85rem;
  }

  @media (max-width: 800px) {
    .privacy-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>
